# Cloudflare Pages cache policy.
# The HTML shell must always be revalidated — a stale cached index.html
# references chunk hashes that no longer exist after a deploy ("Failed to
# fetch dynamically imported module"). Hashed assets are immutable by
# construction, so they can cache forever.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers for every response. The planner is purely static (there is
# no functions/ directory), so Pages applies these to every page and asset.
# HSTS is set at the zone.
#
# Permissions-Policy: /wizard/scan and the AR viewer start immersive-ar
# sessions, which need xr-spatial-tracking, and use the camera; keep the
# screen awake while scanning. Nothing uses location or the microphone.
# Features not listed keep the browser default (same origin only).
#
# The CSP is report-only until a week of reports shows nothing legitimate
# would be blocked. Beyond Supabase and Turnstile it allows what the app
# loads today:
# - fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com: Inter and Outfit (index.html).
# - www.gstatic.com: the Draco decoder for appliance models (ApplianceModel.tsx).
# - raw.githack.com: drei's "apartment" environment map (UnifiedScene.tsx).
# - cdn.jsdelivr.net: troika's font data for drei <Text> labels.
# - scan.bowercabinets.com: staff read customer scan photos from the public
#   scanner (CustomerScanPhotos.tsx); they are shown as blob: images.
# - blob: workers and 'wasm-unsafe-eval': the Draco and meshopt decoders and
#   troika run WebAssembly or scripts inside blob: workers.
# - img-src https:: catalogue and product images come from database rows.
# - 'unsafe-inline' styles: React style attributes and injected toast styles.
#
# Violations go to the csp-report Edge Function, which keeps daily counts in
# public.csp_report_counts (origins and masked paths only). report-to is used
# by browsers with the Reporting API (it needs the planner origin in
# SCANNER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS for the CORS preflight); the others use report-uri.
/*
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), xr-spatial-tracking=(self), screen-wake-lock=(self), geolocation=(), microphone=()
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="https://ehtwywctledgkxexztbh.supabase.co/functions/v1/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://ehtwywctledgkxexztbh.supabase.co https://www.gstatic.com https://raw.githack.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://scan.bowercabinets.com data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; report-uri https://ehtwywctledgkxexztbh.supabase.co/functions/v1/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint

# Quote links carry the job id in the path, so they send no referrer. Pages
# joins a header set by two matching rules with a comma, in file order, and
# browsers apply the last policy they recognise: this rule must stay below /*
# so /quote/* gets "strict-origin-when-cross-origin, no-referrer".
/quote/*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
